B.a7T=new A.j("Shorter","Objective: predict/reduce churn. Method: GBT, AUC 0.86. Data: usage, payments, tickets, terms. Findings: severe tickets matter most; price hikes without value raise churn; early feature adoption cuts churn 22%. Limits: observational. Implications: onboarding nudges, proactive outreach on severe tickets, bundle value with price changes.")
B.a6h=new A.j("More formal","Objective: estimate churn propensity and identify reduction levers. Methodology: gradient-boosted trees (AUC 0.86) on 24 months of labeled outcomes. Principal findings: ticket severity is the strongest predictor; price increases absent additional value elevate risk; early feature adoption (<=14 days) is associated with a 22% churn reduction. Limitations: observational data and potential selection bias. Implications: strengthen onboarding, proactive service for high-severity accounts, and value-bundled price changes.")
B.a8c=new A.j("Add bullets","- Objective: reduce churn via behavioral/billing signals\n- Method: GBT, AUC 0.86\n- Findings: severe tickets top predictor; value-less price hikes raise churn; early feature adoption -22%\n- Limits: observational\n- Implications: onboarding nudges, proactive outreach, bundle value with price changes")
B.a3B=new A.j("Friendlier","In short: we can flag likely churners with good accuracy (AUC 0.86). Severe support issues matter most, price hikes without added value push customers away, and early feature adoption is protective. Let's nudge activation early, jump on severe tickets, and pair any price change with visible value.")
